# Board: two-hats

A board is where task cards are posted, claimed and reported. It holds the bounds every run
on it keeps, whatever hat is worn, and it offers two hats: `note-reader` and `refuse`.

- **keys**: no secret file is read, printed or passed on. The runtime holds it in code, at
  the request (before any model call) and at every tool call.
- **read-only-channel**: the `chat` channel may only read. A request from it that would need
  a change is refused before it is claimed.

The ledger path is relative to this folder. Where the folder is, and which model serves it,
come from runtime config, never from here.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "board",
  "name": "two-hats",
  "supports": ["2026-11-08-draft"],
  "bounds": [
    {
      "id": "keys",
      "rule": "No secret file (.env, a private key, a credentials file) is read, printed or passed on.",
      "at": ["request", "call"]
    },
    {
      "id": "read-only-channel",
      "rule": "A channel declared read-only asks for no change; such a request is refused.",
      "at": ["request"]
    }
  ],
  "profiles": ["profiles/note-reader.us", "profiles/refuse.us"],
  "default_profile": "note-reader",
  "channels": [
    { "name": "console", "may": "change", "cards": true },
    { "name": "chat", "may": "read", "cards": false }
  ],
  "accelerators": 1,
  "unanswered_card": 600,
  "ledger": "run/ledger.jsonl"
}
```
